Closes CNA-FINDINGS A8 -- volumetric fog is enabled by a setting and lit by nothing.

WHAT IS WRONG
  RenderPipeline constructs a VolumetricFogPass, adds it to the chain whenever
  RenderPipelineSettings::getVolumetricFogDensity() is above zero, and never calls setLight on it.
  setLight is public and, from outside, unreachable: the pipeline owns the pass and exposes no
  accessor.

  The pass therefore runs with its own defaults -- VolumetricFogPass.hpp lines 120-122, a null
  shadow map, a direction of (0, -1, 0) and a colour of (1, 0.97, 0.9). That is not "unlit fog".
  It is a march that integrates scattering against a white sun pointing straight down, wherever
  the scene's sun actually is, with nothing shadowing it; and above the rooflines, where the depth
  image has nothing in it, it returns a band of colour across the sky.

WHAT THIS CHANGES
  setShadowScene already receives the light and the shadow map the fog needs, and stores both.
  It now forwards them. A getVolumetricFogPassEXT() accessor is added for the case setShadowScene
  cannot serve: fog with no shadow pass at all, or fog lit by something other than the sun the
  shadows are cast from.

STATE OF THIS PATCH
  Applies cleanly (git apply --check) and the patched translation unit compiles cleanly against the
  patched header, with the exact flags cna-city builds CNA with. It has NOT been run: cnanext is a
  shared checkout and had another session's uncommitted work in modules/platform at the time, so it
  was not modified. The recipe below is what closes that gap.

HOW TO VERIFY IT, FROM THE PROGRAM THAT FOUND IT
  cna-city turns volumetric fog off in RenderPipelineSettings for this reason and says so in
  CityGame::ApplyQuality. To check the fix:

    1. git apply this patch in ../../cnanext
    2. in cna-city, re-enable it: settings.setVolumetricFogDensity(0.015f) at ultra quality
    3. cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
    4. ./build/cna-city --quality ultra --weather fog --fixed-weather --time 7.0 \
                        --camera orbit --screenshot shots/fog.png --frames 400

  Before: a band of red and green across the sky above the rooflines, in fog weather only.
  After: the fog is lit by the same sun the city is, and shadowed by the same cascade -- so it is
  a beam through the streets rather than a wash, and there is nothing above the rooflines.

--- a/modules/graphics-ext/include/CNA/Graphics/RenderPipeline.hpp	2026-08-20 21:14:13.536502649 +0200
+++ b/modules/graphics-ext/include/CNA/Graphics/RenderPipeline.hpp	2026-09-03 19:38:38.267414501 +0200
@@ -259,6 +259,16 @@
                             std::function<void()> drawCasters);
 
         /**
+         * @brief The volumetric fog pass, for a game that lights it itself.
+         *
+         * @ref setShadowScene forwards its light and shadow map here, which is right for the
+         * common case and is what makes the setting usable at all. A game that wants volumetric
+         * fog *without* a shadow pass -- or lit by something other than the sun it casts shadows
+         * from -- has no other way to reach the pass, because the pipeline owns it.
+         */
+        [[nodiscard]] CNAEXT VolumetricFogPass& getVolumetricFogPassEXT();
+
+        /**
          * @brief Supplies a skybox for `begin` to draw behind the scene.
          *
          * plans/plan_modern.md MOD-1104. Drawn immediately after the scene target is bound and cleared,
--- a/modules/graphics-ext/src/RenderPipeline.cpp	2026-08-20 21:14:13.516502649 +0200
+++ b/modules/graphics-ext/src/RenderPipeline.cpp	2026-09-03 19:38:38.267414501 +0200
@@ -480,6 +480,27 @@
         shadowLight_  = light;
         shadowBounds_ = sceneBounds;
         drawCasters_  = std::move(drawCasters);
+
+        // The volumetric fog is lit by this light and blocked by this shadow map, and until now it
+        // was told about neither. VolumetricFogPass::setLight is public and was unreachable: the
+        // pipeline constructs the pass, adds it to the chain whenever the density is above zero,
+        // and never calls it -- so the pass ran with its own defaults, a white light pointing
+        // straight down and no shadow map at all. That is not "no fog": the march integrates
+        // scattering against a sun that has nothing to do with the scene's, unshadowed, and above
+        // the rooflines where the depth image is empty it returns a band of colour across the sky.
+        //
+        // Found by cna-city, which turned the setting on, got the band, and could not turn the
+        // light on from outside. Recorded there as CNA-FINDINGS A8.
+        volumetricFogPass_->setLight(
+            shadowMap, light.Direction,
+            Microsoft::Xna::Framework::Vector3(light.Color.X * light.Intensity,
+                                               light.Color.Y * light.Intensity,
+                                               light.Color.Z * light.Intensity));
+    }
+
+    VolumetricFogPass& RenderPipeline::getVolumetricFogPassEXT()
+    {
+        return *volumetricFogPass_;
     }
 
     bool RenderPipeline::didShadowPassRun() const
